thistle can be cut below the crown. {{smaller|A projection from the back of the blade serves as a fulcrum, by the aid of which the severed plant can be pried up.}}

'''thistle-dollar''' (this′l-dol″är), ''n.'' A Scottish silver coin, also called the ''double merk,'' issued in 1578 by James VI. It weighed 342.6 grains troy, and was worth 23''s.'' 8''d.'' Scotch (nearly 2''s.'' English) at the time of issue.

'''thistle-down''' (this′l-doun), ''n.'' The pappus of the thistle, by which the achenia are borne by the wind to great distances. See cuts under ''thistle.''
